---
const steps = [
  {
    title: 'Discover',
    text: 'Map the workflow, baseline human performance, pressure-test build-vs-buy, and produce a fixed-scope statement of work. If AI is the wrong lever, we say so.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Build',
    text: 'Ship a thin production slice on real traffic early, then expand. Models, retrieval, agents, integrations, evals, and observability — owned by your team.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Run',
    text: 'Monitor KPIs against baseline, refresh prompts as data drifts, tune reviewer thresholds, and train your operators so the system keeps paying off.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="process-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="section__eyebrow">Engagement model</p>
    <h2 id="process-heading">Discover. Build. Run.</h2>
    <p class="answer">
      AviKaiDo engagements follow a three-phase model so strategy and delivery stay with the same
      accountable builder. Each phase is a separate decision: take the artifacts in-house after any
      one of them, or continue into production operations.
    </p>
    <ol class="process-steps">
      {
        steps.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <h3>{s.title}</h3>
            <p>{s.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
